  "description": "Trade Alert for Portfolio USA",
  "body_html": "<p></p><div><hr></div><p><strong>Trade Alert:</strong> Buy ARQT for Portfolio USA</p><div><hr></div><p>Arcutis Biotherapeutics (NASDAQ: ARQT) looks pretty tempting right now. Here's the quick and dirty on why:</p><p>They've got ZORYVE, an award-winning dermatological cream that's delivering impressive results—basically, it's an anti-inflammatory superstar that kicks steroidal creams to the curb. The big plus? It can be safely used long-term, unlike traditional steroid-based treatments, which are huge for chronic sufferers. Revenue jumped a ridiculous 471% year-over-year in Q4, and that momentum isn't likely to stop anytime soon, especially with more FDA approvals expected in 2025.</p><p>On top of that, strategic partnerships—like the deal with Kowa Pharmaceuticals—are set to broaden their market dramatically. They're pushing into the massive Medicaid and Medicare patient segments (about 4 million patients), plus tapping into another 8.5 million patients through primary care and pediatric channels. Not bad for a company that's still considered relatively niche.</p><p>Financially, ARQT is pretty solid too. Sure, they reported negative EPS, but it's significantly improving each quarter, hinting strongly at profitability by 2026. They also recently wiped out $100M of debt, freeing up their balance sheet for future growth.</p><p>Analysts seem to agree—five upward revisions in the last three months with zero going the other way speaks volumes. Despite potential risks like regulatory hurdles, competitive pressure, or heavy reliance on a single flagship product (ZORYVE), Arcutis is impressively executing on its growth strategy.</p>",
